WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.954
He was one of the biggest movie stars in the 1990s.

2
00:00:05.955 --> 00:00:12.951
So why did he live in a small, dirty home that was polluted with his own waste?

3
00:00:12.952 --> 00:00:22.675
He was also underweight and had terrible tooth and skin problems—not very attractive for a world-famous actor. But

4
00:00:22.676 --> 00:00:30.360
few people knew the sad truth about Keiko, the killer whale. Killer

5
00:00:30.361 --> 00:00:35.847
whales, also known as "orcas," are found in oceans around the world. Keiko

6
00:00:35.848 --> 00:00:40.640
was born in the Atlantic, off the coast of Iceland. At

7
00:00:40.641 --> 00:00:48.269
around age two, Keiko was captured by a crew aboard a fishing boat and taken to an aquarium. A

8
00:00:48.270 --> 00:00:53.384
few years later he was sold to a water park in Canada. There,

9
00:00:53.385 --> 00:00:58.276
Keiko began training to be a performer. Then

10
00:00:58.277 --> 00:01:02.511
he was sold to an amusement park in Mexico. For

11
00:01:02.512 --> 00:01:09.041
the next ten years, Keiko starred in over seven thousand performances at the park. He

12
00:01:09.042 --> 00:01:15.820
was hand-fed about sixty kilograms of dead fish each day. But

13
00:01:15.821 --> 00:01:20.471
his pool was too small, and Keiko was bored. His

14
00:01:20.472 --> 00:01:26.164
dorsal fin, located on his back, was droopy. This

15
00:01:26.165 --> 00:01:36.462
meant Keiko was spending too much time on the surface of the water and swimming in only one direction. However,

16
00:01:36.463 --> 00:01:44.409
most audiences were not aware of Keiko’s poor living conditions. In

17
00:01:44.410 --> 00:01:51.573
1993, when Keiko starred in the movie Free Willy , his life changed forever.

18
00:01:51.574 --> 00:01:56.629
Free Willy is about a boy and a water-park whale named Willy.

19
00:01:56.630 --> 00:02:03.999
The boy, who is deeply attached to Willy, finds out that Willy’s owners are planning to kill the whale.

20
00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:11.471
The boy does everything he can to save, and eventually free, Willy.

21
00:02:11.472 --> 00:02:17.784
The movie was a big hit and touched audiences everywhere.

22
00:02:17.785 --> 00:02:23.055
It also led many people to think about Keiko's real-life situation.

23
00:02:23.056 --> 00:02:32.682
In 1994 the Free Willy-Keiko Foundation was established to rescue Keiko and release him back into the wild.

24
00:02:32.683 --> 00:02:40.681
Thousands of children from around the world also campaigned for Keiko’s freedom.

25
00:02:40.682 --> 00:02:47.285
They wrote letters to politicians and raised money.

26
00:02:47.286 --> 00:02:53.870
At last the amusement park in Mexico agreed to donate Keiko to the foundation.

27
00:02:53.871 --> 00:02:57.748
The foundation planned to return Keiko to the wild.

28
00:02:57.749 --> 00:03:01.504
But first they had to teach him how to live there.

29
00:03:01.505 --> 00:03:05.757
They built a new home for Keiko in the United States.

30
00:03:05.758 --> 00:03:10.489
But how could they move a seven-thousand-pound killer whale?

31
00:03:10.490 --> 00:03:18.360
UPS, a package delivery service, volunteered to move Keiko to his new home.

32
00:03:18.361 --> 00:03:23.979
Keiko’s new home in Oregon was a large, custom-made pool by the ocean.

33
00:03:23.980 --> 00:03:31.329
There, for the first time in many years, Keiko swam in natural seawater.

34
00:03:31.330 --> 00:03:36.834
Ten dedicated trainers helped Keiko learn how to live in the wild again.

35
00:03:36.835 --> 00:03:43.666
Killer whales in the wild often swim as much as 160 kilometers every day.

36
00:03:43.667 --> 00:03:51.488
Each day Keiko had to swim farther and faster than before.

37
00:03:51.489 --> 00:03:57.858
As he improved and grew stronger, the trainers encouraged and rewarded him.

38
00:03:57.859 --> 00:04:02.814
Keiko especially liked to get his back and fins rubbed.

39
00:04:02.815 --> 00:04:08.305
It was also important for Keiko to learn how to catch his own food.

40
00:04:08.306 --> 00:04:11.242
The trainers put live fish into the water.

41
00:04:11.243 --> 00:04:18.181
At first Keiko would catch a fish and then release it.

42
00:04:18.182 --> 00:04:22.917
He had to be taught to eat the live fish after he caught them!

43
00:04:22.918 --> 00:04:28.266
For about a year, Keiko learned how to live in the wild.

44
00:04:28.267 --> 00:04:32.435
He gained weight and his skin problems vanished.

45
00:04:32.436 --> 00:04:37.210
But best of all, his dorsal fin began to uncurl.

46
00:04:37.211 --> 00:04:41.989
That meant Keiko was doing just fine.

47
00:04:41.990 --> 00:04:46.590
Killer whales are very close to their families.

48
00:04:46.591 --> 00:04:53.276
The trainers thought Keiko should return to his birthplace, where he might reunite with his family.

49
00:04:53.277 --> 00:04:59.385
After two years in the U.S., Keiko was taken back to Iceland.

50
00:04:59.386 --> 00:05:04.646
For almost twenty years, Keiko had been dependent on humans.

51
00:05:04.647 --> 00:05:09.500
Now he would have to survive on his own in a natural environment.

52
00:05:09.501 --> 00:05:14.062
The trainers slowly helped Keiko adjust to his new home.

53
00:05:14.074 --> 00:05:20.734
They allowed Keiko to go into the sea for an hour or two and followed him in small boats.

54
00:05:20.735 --> 00:05:24.777
Then they would direct him back to a pen.

55
00:05:24.778 --> 00:05:30.767
They gradually increased the time Keiko spent in the ocean.

56
00:05:30.768 --> 00:05:37.025
Soon Keiko was behaving like a wild killer whale.

57
00:05:37.026 --> 00:05:42.263
He spent more time underwater than on the surface.

58
00:05:42.264 --> 00:05:46.670
He began competing with other animals for food.

59
00:05:46.671 --> 00:05:54.046
He even made contact with wild killer whales near his pen by calling out to them.

60
00:05:54.047 --> 00:05:58.450
The trainers continued to monitor his progress.

61
00:05:58.451 --> 00:06:04.545
At last, in 2002 Keiko was released.

62
00:06:04.546 --> 00:06:12.397
Strong and free, he swam about 1,400 kilometers to Norway’s coast.

63
00:06:12.398 --> 00:06:20.938
Thanks to the hard work of caring people, Keiko finally got to live as a killer whale should.

64
00:06:20.939 --> 00:06:26.172
In December 2003 Keiko died of an illness.

65
00:06:26.173 --> 00:06:39.114
But the killer whale who brought warmth and joy to the hearts of millions around the world will always be remembered.

